Rocket Counter (Fabric client mod, Minecraft 1.21.11)

Shows a list in the top-left corner of every nearby player holding firework
rockets, with the stack size and an "(elytra)" tag if they wear one.

EASIEST WAY TO GET THE JAR (no Java or Gradle on your PC):
1. Make a free GitHub account and create a new repository.
2. Upload everything in this folder to it (including the hidden .github folder).
3. Open the repo's "Actions" tab and wait for "Build mod jar" to finish (~2 min).
4. Open that run and download the "rocketcounter-jar" artifact. Unzip it:
   rocketcounter-1.0.0.jar is your mod.
5. Put that jar and Fabric API in your .minecraft/mods folder
   (Fabric Loader installed for 1.21.11). Client only; servers don't need it.

If the build fails, open the failed run, copy the error and send it to me.

BUILDING LOCALLY INSTEAD:
JDK 21, then "gradle build" (or copy the Gradle wrapper from the
fabric-example-mod repo, 1.21.11 branch, and run ./gradlew build).
The jar ends up in build/libs/.

Check the versions in gradle.properties against https://fabricmc.net/develop

pluginManagement {
	repositories {
		maven { name = 'Fabric'; url = 'https://maven.fabricmc.net/' }
		mavenCentral()
		gradlePluginPortal()
	}
}

.gradle/
build/
run/
.idea/
*.iml

plugins {
	id 'fabric-loom' version "${loom_version}"
	id 'maven-publish'
}

version = project.mod_version
group = project.maven_group

base {
	archivesName = project.archives_base_name
}

dependencies {
	minecraft "com.mojang:minecraft:${project.minecraft_version}"
	// 1.21.11 is still obfuscated; Yarn is discontinued, so use Mojang's names.
	mappings loom.officialMojangMappings()
	modImplementation "net.fabricmc:fabric-loader:${project.loader_version}"
	modImplementation "net.fabricmc.fabric-api:fabric-api:${project.fabric_api_version}"
}

processResources {
	inputs.property "version", project.version
	filesMatching("fabric.mod.json") {
		expand "version": inputs.properties.version
	}
}

tasks.withType(JavaCompile).configureEach {
	it.options.release = 21
}

java {
	withSourcesJar()
	sourceCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_21
	targetCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_21
}
